<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5.1 Multilingual Calibration Methods ‣ 5 Improving Multilingual Calibration ‣ Beyond the Final Layer: Intermediate Representations for Better Multilingual Calibration in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Experiment Setup</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS2" title="In 5 Improving Multilingual Calibration ‣ Beyond the Final Layer: Intermediate Representations for Better Multilingual Calibration in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5.2 </span>Calibration Results</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5.2 Calibration Results ‣ 5 Improving Multilingual Calibration ‣ Beyond the Final Layer: Intermediate Representations for Better Multilingual Calibration in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Intermediate-layer confidence shows better calibration than final-layer confidence.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5.2 Calibration Results ‣ 5 Improving Multilingual Calibration ‣ Beyond the Final Layer: Intermediate Representations for Better Multilingual Calibration in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Classical post-hoc methods offer improvements but face challenges in multilingual settings.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5.2 Calibration Results ‣ 5 Improving Multilingual Calibration ‣ Beyond the Final Layer: Intermediate Representations for Better Multilingual Calibration in Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">LACE is complementary to post-hoc approaches and delivers the best calibration performance.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
